  "narrative": "The independent validation for H24 strongly supports the TP53-loss/USP7 association. H24 has direction +1, so the reported signed estimates are raw exposed-minus-comparator differences on the dependency_USP7 scale. Discovery was +0.396 with 95% interval +0.325 to +0.467. Validation was +0.437 with independent interval +0.336 to +0.537. Because this is a direction +1 claim, a positive value means TP53-loss cells have higher, less-negative USP7 dependency scores than TP53-intact cells, i.e. weaker USP7 dependency. The magnitude is far larger than a roughly 10% relative effect threshold and remains bounded away from zero even under the stringent validation interval, so I accept H24 as a robust dataset-specific association. This does not establish causality or generalizability beyond the supplied dataset; it establishes that the association is stable within the supplied experimental system and validation split. I keep H24 active because context and specificity analyses remain useful. The prior POLR2A specificity controls for SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high, PTEN loss, and KEAP1 loss had very small point estimates relative to the large accepted associations, reducing concern about generic screen or cell-state confounding, but the TP53-loss POLR2A control H26 is still pending. The newly registered interactions ask whether accepted associations are stable across measured contexts: SMARCA4-loss effect by ARID1A loss for SMARCA2, PTEN-loss effect by PIK3CA mutation for STAT3, MSI-high effect by lineage subtype for WRN, and KEAP1-loss effect by STK11 loss for NFE2L2. The new USP7 cross-specificity proposals test whether SMARCA4 loss or PTEN loss also produce TP53-like USP7 effects. If those controls are large, I would downgrade the apparent specificity of the corresponding accepted associations; if they are near null, the accepted associations become more credible as dataset-specific, predictor-specific patterns. The next most informative analyses are therefore H26 and H27 plus these context/specificity proposals.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 2 synthesis update after corrected form. Accepted dataset-specific associations: H6 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H11 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency; H17 KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative NFE2L2 dependency; H24 TP53 loss -> weaker/less-negative USP7 dependency. H24 is now independently validated: discovery signed +0.396 CI +0.325/+0.467; validation signed +0.437 CI +0.336/+0.537. This supports reliability within this dataset/validation split, not causality or external generalizability. Rejected/closed controls and nearby nulls: H2 BRAF/BRAF, H3 EGFR amp/EGFR after validation, H5 original KEAP1 direction, H10 MYC/DHX9, H13 KRAS/RIT1, H14 TP53/RPL11, H15 MYC/KIF18A, H16 EGFR/TMED10, H22 ARID1A/SMARCA2, H23 PIK3CA/STAT3, H25 KRAS-context EGFR. Deferred weak unresolved: H1 KRAS/KRAS, H4 ERBB2/ERBB2, H8 TP53/MDM2, H9 MYC/USP7; technical control H12 unresolved closed. POLR2A specificity controls H18-H21 have tiny point estimates relative to accepted biological effects, but H26 TP53 POLR2A control remains pending. Next analyses should include H26 and H27 plus new context/specificity proposals: SMARCA4 loss by ARID1A loss for SMARCA2; PTEN loss by PIK3CA mutation for STAT3; MSI-high by lineage subtype for WRN; KEAP1 loss by STK11 loss for NFE2L2; USP7 with SMARCA4 loss or PTEN loss as specificity controls; WRN with SMARCA4 loss and SMARCA2 with PTEN loss as cross-specificity checks. Interpret large interactions as context dependence, not reversal of main effects unless subgroup contrasts themselves are clear. If cross-specificity or POLR2A controls are large, reassess specificity of the corresponding accepted association. Keep all claims dataset-specific until independent external evidence exists."
